# Selectors

Functions in `selectors.py` use the same `<entity>_<action>` names, keyword-only arguments, and type hints as services. Selectors only read. List filters are applied inside the selector. The endpoint validates query parameters and passes them in.

```python
# ❌ BAD — the endpoint filters the queryset
@router.get("/users", response=list[UserOut])
def user_list(request, email: str | None = None):
    qs = User.objects.all()
    if email:
        qs = qs.filter(email=email)
    return qs

# ✅ GOOD
def user_list(*, email: str | None = None) -> QuerySet[User]:
    qs = User.objects.all()
    if email is not None:
        qs = qs.filter(email=email)
    return qs
```
